  "body": "*Originally sent in the element-web repository, but I was told that it's a synapse bug https://github.com/vector-im/element-web/issues/20190 *\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Run an export on an old room (in my case the [Invidious](https://invidious.io/) room [#invidious:matrix.org](https://matrix.to/#/#invidious:matrix.org) )\r\n2. Choose JSON and 4MB\r\n3. Run an export, until it get stuck, looks at the console: 403\r\n\r\n\r\n### Outcome\r\n\r\n#### What did you expect?\r\n\r\nSkips the 403, or just don't 403\r\n\r\n#### What happened instead?\r\n![this](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/47571719/146059979-9df3e412-f85c-4a02-94d6-83387cf2911b.png)\r\n\r\nThen stops.\r\n\r\nIf I restart the export again, it give a 403 instantly, however if I clear the cache of the client, it works, until this error happens again.\r\n\r\nNote:\r\n\r\nIt's an old V1 room (from early 2019), we want to export it so that we can upgrade it while keeping a backup of the messages.\r\n\r\nWe did an HTML export with attachment an hour before without issue.\r\n\r\nit's maybe a Synapse issue.\r\n\r\n### Operating system\r\n\r\nDebian\r\n\r\n### Application version\r\n\r\n1.9.7\r\n\r\n### How did you install the app?\r\n\r\nOfficial Element repository\r\n\r\n### Homeserver\r\n\r\nMy own\r\n\r\n### Will you send logs?\r\n\r\nNo",
